Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.44,Default,,0,0,0,,An assistant saying done is not proof. AIGON PROOF gives each action an exact review,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.44,0:00:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,an authenticated approval, and a receipt for the work actually performed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.26,0:00:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,First, a client contract is addressed to an external partner. The server knows the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.09,0:00:26.24,Default,,0,0,0,,document contains personal data. It blocks the action. Even an operator cannot
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.24,0:00:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,approve this policy violation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.93,0:00:35.05,Default,,0,0,0,,We explicitly choose the anonymised summary instead. The document and recipient are
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.05,0:00:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,shown before approval. Nothing in this command invents consent or silently changes
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.97,0:00:42.45,Default,,0,0,0,,the trust boundary.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.19,0:00:48.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The operator unlocks approval with a private credential. That credential is never
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.89,0:00:52.11,Default,,0,0,0,,part of the agent's command or passport.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.85,0:00:59.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Approve once records who approved the exact action fingerprint. The server now signs
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.24,0:01:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,a short-lived passport. This is permission, not a delivery claim.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.57,0:01:11.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Changing the recipient invalidates the authorization. The original approved action
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.07,0:01:13.14,Default,,0,0,0,,remains available to execute.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.87,0:01:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Execute performs the work. The server writes actual document bytes into the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.10,0:01:26.86,Default,,0,0,0,,recipient's local inbox, reads them back, verifies their SHA-256 hash, and persists
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.86,0:01:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,this receipt.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.49,0:01:34.91,Default,,0,0,0,,A second execution is rejected. One human approval cannot be reused through another
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.91,0:01:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,passport either.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.98,0:01:42.42,Default,,0,0,0,,After restarting the server, the receipt history is still here. Approval and replay
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.42,0:01:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,records are durable, not just browser state.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.05,0:01:52.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The operator can also deny or revoke an action. A denial does not produce a usable
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.87,0:01:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,passport.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.52,0:02:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Six negative policy probes check forged approval, sensitive egress and unknown
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.79,0:02:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,parameters. The demonstration also exercises real recipient tampering and replay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.76,0:02:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The same Rust service exposes the governance explorer and MCP protocol 2025-11-25.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.67,0:02:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,AIGON PROOF: approve the action, verify the outcome.
